From 40e96ef231579c528de26d2003e86e1a3ddca89b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Parada <livercake@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:50:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] MUSEUM FIX (2026-09-29): wrap osd_message for Beetle PSX
 analog OSD smosh

Beetle PSX (mednafen_psx) reports its DualShock analog toggle via
osd_message() -> RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_MESSAGE_EXT, which RetroArch bakes
into the canvas frame as gfx-widget text. That is unreachable from EJS's
DOM displayMessage and unskinnable from CSS, so visitors get a canvas-
burned "DualShock on port N: Analog|Digital Mode" toast they cannot read.

The core option beetle_psx_display_osd is all-or-nothing (it would also
kill real error OSD), so museum_osd_wrap.c wraps the symbol at link time
(-Wl,--wrap=osd_message, scoped to mednafen_psx* targets). Analog/Digital
mode messages are forwarded to the parent window as coreMessage posts
(EmulatorOverlay renders them via showToast) and suppressed canvas-side;
everything else falls through to the real implementation via a "%s"
forward, so error/FPS OSD is byte-identical.

Remap-proof: the core stays the source of truth, no JS combo tracking.
Relink-only on refresh (no core recompile); verify coreMessage appears
exactly once in each variant's glue JS after relinking.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 museum_osd_wrap.c | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 museum_osd_wrap.c

diff --git a/museum_osd_wrap.c b/museum_osd_wrap.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..6b472801b6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/museum_osd_wrap.c
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+/* MUSEUM FIX (analog OSD smosh): pillow-smosh Beetle's canvas-drawn OSD
+ * toasts into the parent's .iframe-toast pill.
+ *
+ * Beetle reports its DualShock analog toggle ("DualShock on port N:
+ * Analog|Digital Mode") via osd_message() -> RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_MESSAGE_EXT,
+ * which RetroArch renders as gfx-widget text baked into the canvas frame --
+ * unreachable from EJS's DOM displayMessage and unskinnable from CSS. The
+ * core option beetle_psx_display_osd is all-or-nothing (it would also kill
+ * real error OSD), so instead this file wraps the symbol at link time
+ * (-Wl,--wrap=osd_message, scoped to mednafen_psx* targets below): analog
+ * mode messages are forwarded to the parent window as coreMessage posts
+ * (EmulatorOverlay renders them through showToast) and suppressed
+ * canvas-side; every other message falls through to the real implementation
+ * via a "%s" forward, so error/FPS OSD is byte-identical.
+ *
+ * Match rule: contains "Analog"|"Digital" AND capital-M "Mode". The
+ * capital M excludes neGcon's "mode is ON/OFF" (lowercase, kept on canvas;
+ * no beetle-PSX gun games exist in the library anyway).
+ *
+ * Called on the main thread (retro_run input poll), so EM_ASM is safe.
+ * `parent` here is the iframe's parent -- the museum page -- whose message
+ * handler already validates e.source and renders coreMessage via showToast.
+ */
+#include <emscripten.h>
+#include <stdarg.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+void __real_osd_message(unsigned priority, int level, int target, int type,
+                        const char *format, ...);
+
+void __wrap_osd_message(unsigned priority, int level, int target, int type,
+                        const char *format, ...)
+{
+   char buf[4096];
+   va_list ap;
+
+   va_start(ap, format);
+   vsnprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), format, ap);
+   va_end(ap);
+
+   if ((strstr(buf, "Analog") || strstr(buf, "Digital")) &&
+       strstr(buf, "Mode")) {
+      EM_ASM({ parent.postMessage({ type: 'coreMessage', text: UTF8ToString($0) }, '*'); }, buf);
+      return;
+   }
+   __real_osd_message(priority, level, target, type, "%s", buf);
+}
